Riley face to face with a terrifying secret."

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.940
The eyes of the undead also look very similar
to the True Knot and it’s clear for Flanagan

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:44.620
that there’s a lot at STAKE here.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:53.510
Now we open on the symbol of the ichthus which
was created after Christ multiplied fish and

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:57.090
loaves of breads in order to feed far more
people than they should have been able to.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:02.240
This idea of symbol tied to Christianity is
quickly juxtaposed by the horrific crash that

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.049
kick starts the season and it subtly sets
up the idea that we will be facing several

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:09.789
themes such as religion which will be interlaced
with death.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:14.130
In real life we've seen the horrors of what
religion can lead to in the likes of Jones

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:19.030
Town which similar to season ended up with
those indoctrinated sipping the Cool Aid after

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.950
they heard the promise of a better life.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:26.400
It all begins with Riley a man who caused
a catastrophic car crash thanks to his drinking

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.490
which lead to the death of a young lady named
Tara Beth.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.370
After serving four years in prison he's sentenced
to serve parole and he returns home to Crockett

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:37.930
Island, a backwards fishing community struggling
to stay relevant in an ever changing world.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.920
Riley attempted to escape his life destined
to be a fisherman by entering the world of

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.090
tech, but alas, he would end up back from
whence he came.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:50.170
He’s an atheist, having read every single
religious text from every religion Riley very

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:54.319
much sees life as a waste of time that sucks
worse than a Vampire.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:03:00.209
This is what makes this show so layered and
no that's not a garlic pun...or is it onions.

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:06.410
Now usually religious horror is explored simply
through the eyes of Christianity, but in this,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.060
many different view points are explored from
Riley’s Atheism.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.490
There's a lot of examples such as a Sheriff's
unwavering belief in honour of his wife in

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:18.670
Islam and Bev, a Delores Umbridge-esque do
gooder who carries a hatred of anything that

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.150
isn’t Christian.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.930
Riley is clearly wracked with guilt and over
the course of the series he must come to terms

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.900
with what he did, and his own mortality as
well as how his family and neighbours view

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.900
him.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.910
He returns home to his family and tries to
adjust to life on the island but Tara Beth

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.780
watches over him, never letting him forget.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.099
At night he dreams that he's out on a boat
in the middle of the ocean and we'll talk

00:03:37.099 --> 00:03:41.750
about how the idea of life being but a dream
is paid off in this imagery later on.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:46.000
Life on the island mainly focuses around the
church, St Patricks and the core faith of

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.040
each character is explored in great detail.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.640
Spooks and jump scares are swapped for lengthy
monologues and discussions which are delivered

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.900
expertly.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.790
Faith is key as the show rumbles on as we
meet each character such as Sheriff Hassan,

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.080
an NYPD veteran, pushed out due to racism.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.099
Erin who wants to embrace religion and her
home once more as well as a mysterious new

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:10.470
priest called father Paul who arrives after
telling us that the last one fell gravely

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.470
ill.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:16.549
Now as soon as I saw the large chest and cats
being eaten I said that it would be f**king

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:17.549
Vampires.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:21.320
Those who've read Bram Stoker's Dracula will
know that the vampire arrived on the coast

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.850
of Whitby in England through a chest just
like this and if you've visited the fishing

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.000
village you'll know it's a similar sort of
set up to what we see in the show.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.010
The Cathedral there looms over the entire
area much like the church in this and though

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:37.440
Flannagan isn't beating us over the head with
references it's clear he's giving nods to

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.110
the most famous Vampire story of all time.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.780
Paul is later revealed to be Pruitt who traveled
on a religious pilgrimage but due to his dementia

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.830
he got lost and came across a Vampire.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:51.830
Believing it was an angel he cried out for
help and the beast fed him his blood which

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.070
restored his health and healed him.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:57.729
It's important to note that communion is very
much seen as drinking the blood of Christ

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:01.240
and again it's sort of like Poetry they rhyme.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.509
Vampire of course need familiars in order
to travel out into the Sun and Pruitt very

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:07.520
much becomes the Angels.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.160
Now upon his return to the island it’s hinted
that we are facing the end of days as a gigantic

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.710
storm rolls in.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:18.070
The rain washes up the bodies of cats across
the beach which is reminiscent of the infamous

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:22.310
plagues and Riley is adamant that he had seen
Monsignor Pruit which is brushed away as being

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.750
shadows in the dark.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:29.000
Paul or should I call him Pruitt starts mass,
explaining how the island will rise again

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.320
and over time he becomes a popular figure
on the island.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.320
I love how this seems like just empty words
and faith at face value except he does have

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.320
a plan in that he wants to use the blood of
the angel and well to change the fortunes

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.320
of the island.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.949
Many are down on their luck including Leeza
who was paralysed by the town drunk Joe who,

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:38.840
like Riley and Hasan is seen as an outsider.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:39.840
The treatment of those in need but not seen
as socially acceptable like Joe by Bev shows

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.840
the nasty, selective side of religious people.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.300
Though it's never confirmed, Bev ends up poisoning
Joe's Dog and it seems like she kills Paul

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.330
too which resurrects him.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:51.110
We never get this for definite but he seems
to die much like the dog does with blood coming

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:55.009
out of his mouth and of course let me know
below if you disagree.

00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:59.000
In the series we learn that if one dies whilst
the Angel's blood is within their system then

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.139
they'll rise up as a Vampire that wants to
feast on human flesh.

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:06.820
There's a lot of people confused over why
Paul could handle the light early on but at

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:12.080
this point he wasn't technically a vampire,
he just had the vampire's blood in his system.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.669
Now Bev mentioned that the Bible speaks of
angels with burning skin in Revelation and

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:19.320
both she and Paul use this to justify their
actions throughout the show.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.320
The pair cherry-pick scripture moving away
from the bibles altruistic messages and though

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.320
she seems to Paul despite when he changes
his mind at the end, she pulls out more scripture

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.320
that justifies her turning her back on him.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.320
The idea of the angels in Midnight Mass comes
from the notion that the myth of vampires

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.320
and angels derives from an oral history that
evolved into the myth we know today.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.320
When revealed to her what has happened and
what the angels do by feeding on blood, Sarah

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.699
surmises that the myths of these angels could
come from a blood disease that creates a drastic

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:27.699
need for iron.

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:28.699
Of course the idea of these angels is incredibly
similar to vampires but Christian ritual and

00:06:28.699 --> 00:06:29.699
belief could be explained by these beings.

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:32.550
The sacrament asks worshippers to take wine
said to be the blood of Christ and he himself

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.160
died and came back three days later.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:39.440
Sarah quite rightly explains this is indeed
where the Christian ritual could come from.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:45.290
Sharing his blood would mean empowering and
curing people, explaining the miracles from

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.290
the Bible.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.979
Pruitt has a plan for improving their life
by continuing to use the tainted angel blood

00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:54.430
for the sacramental wine, regenerating the
cells of those that come to Church.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.410
He intends to make everyone’s life better
and the healing properties of it allow Leeza

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.710
to walk again.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.789
This Miracle brings more people to the Church
and thus it gives Paul a bigger flock to infect.

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:10.100
Hints start to show that something peculiar
is going on, as people start visibly healing.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:14.720
Riley’s dad back mends itself, his wife
no longer needs glasses and she starts to

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.260
look young and Sarah’s Mother basically
does a Benjamin Button down that blouse you

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.260
Gilf.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:21.919
Now It seems Flanagan has replaced hidden
ghosts for hidden heals and though it initally

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:26.480
seems like good news it also has adverse effects
in that it kills Erin's baby.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:31.800
Atheism and faith in an era of miracles is
explored in great detail with Hassan struggling

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.790
to get his child to follow Islam, as Ali wants
to fit in and choose his faith, making this

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.930
a multilayered exploration of what it is to
believe.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:45.169
Bev is vile towards the religion and only
becomes more and more emboldened as her idolisation

00:07:45.169 --> 00:07:49.120
of Paul increases, someone she was dismissive
of at first.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:54.340
After his death Paul starts jonesing hard
and he kills Joe before drinking his blood.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.020
This happens after he points out the similarities
between Paul and a Young Pruitt and also pays

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:03.500
lip service to the affair that the latter
was apparently having with Sarah's mother.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.080
Another hint towards an eventual reveal comes
when she said she thought she saw Sarah's

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.880
dads face at her bedroom window but this is
brushed away as being a side effect of her

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:12.880
demention.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.740
Later on it's revealed that Paul is indeed
Sarah's father and we learn he was peering

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.199
into houses which was set up nicely in that
moment.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:26.460
Bev involves other town members, namely Sturge
and Leeza's father and slowly everyone begins

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:30.740
to get their hands dirty in order to keep
up the sanctity of Church.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:35.449
One night Riley on a chance encounter turns
up at the rec centre and sees Paul pouring

00:08:35.449 --> 00:08:38.360
angel blood into the sacrament and Mr X, sorry
the angel who kills him and turns him into

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.389
a creature of the night.

00:08:39.389 --> 00:08:43.789
If there was one core message I took away
from this show it is that not everyone is

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.089
as virtuous as they claim to be.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:51.959
Paul explains to Riley what happened and urges
him to remember him by telling a story about

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:56.300
an altar boy who brought him a dying rat which
turns out to be Riley.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.949
Pruitt lied to instill Riley’s faith leading
Riley to then have unrealistic expectations

00:09:00.949 --> 00:09:03.449
growing up that he has now stepped away from.

00:09:03.449 --> 00:09:07.620
There's an incredible scene with both Riley
and Erin in which they talk about what they

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.410
imagine death to be.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:13.990
Because of his distrust of church the former
very much sees nothing at the end whereas

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:19.899
Erin who is grieving her baby imagines being
embraced by her family in the afterlife.

00:09:19.899 --> 00:09:24.199
When Erin dies in the show she changes this
thinking and instead views herself as simply

00:09:24.199 --> 00:09:29.100
a manifestation of the universe dreaming of
itself and what life would be like.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:33.254
Einstein famously said that energy can neither
be created or destroyed and we are all simply

00:09:33.254 --> 00:09:34.254
here and then gone back into the greater whole.

00:09:34.254 --> 00:09:35.300
She summises The energy that happens when
her brain is firing must come from somewhere

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.449
and she sees this as simply being absorbed
back into the everything upon passing away.

00:09:37.449 --> 00:09:41.739
Our consciousness came from seemingly nowhere
but we all have our own thougths and feelings

00:09:41.739 --> 00:09:46.089
and when we cease to exist we will return
to whatever we were before.

00:09:46.089 --> 00:09:50.630
It's a beautiful conversation and it somewhat
foreshadows Riley's death which comes not

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:51.939
long after.

00:09:51.939 --> 00:09:56.679
Paul explains he wants to heal the community
but really he’s a self serving person who

00:09:56.679 --> 00:09:59.869
has just accepted these awful things that
need to happen, citing scripture as a good

00:09:59.869 --> 00:10:00.869
reason.

00:10:00.869 --> 00:10:05.610
Paul intends for people to convert to being
an angel and be welcomed peacefully into this

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.880
new life but they will all very much be forced
to follow what he says.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:09.880
Riley manages to break free and Paul lets
him, which just felt a bit misguided and naive

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.880
of Pruitt and eventually this constant faith
in him being correct about everything is what

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.880
leads to his downfall.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.939
With Erin, Riley heads out onto the ocean
and explains that this is very reminiscent

00:10:13.939 --> 00:10:14.939
of his dream.

00:10:14.939 --> 00:10:19.299
He finally finds his purpose and Riley to
me is someone who had two options.

00:10:19.299 --> 00:10:23.379
He could live for eternity as a self serving
vampire that would feed upon others to get

00:10:23.379 --> 00:10:28.230
his wish or he could finally break free of
this and avoid hurting the ones that he loved.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:33.410
Alcoholism, especially drunk driving is often
seen as a very self centred act and the character

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.809
doing this in the intro led to the death of
an innocent woman.

00:10:36.809 --> 00:10:41.179
However it also hurt his family on top of
it and because of this he's lived a life of

00:10:41.179 --> 00:10:42.369
misery.

00:10:42.369 --> 00:10:47.619
Riley could easily feast upon Erin at this
point but instead he burns himself and gives

00:10:47.619 --> 00:10:50.889
her the knowledge that he needs to take down
Pruitt and his followers.

00:10:50.889 --> 00:10:55.619
This to me is why he's joined by the spirit
of Tara Beth at the end who has clearly forgiven

00:10:55.619 --> 00:10:58.050
him because he learned from his mistakes.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.579
Rather than being alone on the boat as he
was he has his greatest mistake forgiving

00:11:01.579 --> 00:11:08.309
him and thus he can forgive himself as he
passes away...in a beautif...oh myyyyy goood

00:11:08.309 --> 00:11:11.619
this is absolutel horrific.

00:11:11.619 --> 00:11:15.470
Now Erin returns back to the island as the
night time mass is being prepared for easter

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:16.470
vigil.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:20.429
This is one of the most popular times for
church attendance and thus he can recruit

00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:22.029
more to the cause.

00:11:22.029 --> 00:11:26.369
However Easter itself is also about the death
and rebirth of Christ which is a theme that

00:11:26.369 --> 00:11:28.019
is used at the ceremony.

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:32.079
Erin plans to work with Sarah and her mother
to stop the converted however it ultimately

00:11:32.079 --> 00:11:34.709
fails as they fall in line and head to the
church.

00:11:34.709 --> 00:11:35.709
Fire is a very suitable idea and metaphor
to kill the angels and converted which is

00:11:35.709 --> 00:11:36.709
used heavily later in the show as Sarah attempts
to burn down the church.

00:11:36.709 --> 00:11:37.709
Fire in the bible is often used for purification
which fits in with these people who want to

00:11:37.709 --> 00:11:38.709
wipe the island of those that don’t fall
in line.

00:11:38.709 --> 00:11:39.769
At The church the attendees are offered up
a cup filled with Bev's poison and most of

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:42.639
them willingly end their lives in order to
be reborn.

00:11:42.639 --> 00:11:47.480
However they're hungry for flesh and the undead
turn on the living which leads to a blood

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.480
bath.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:52.560
Bev heads out into the night with the newly
converted and they cast judgement on all,

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.320
killing all of the islanders.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:58.509
We see some of the best sequences in the show
as the rabid angels go around feeding and

00:11:58.509 --> 00:12:02.550
burn everything to the ground believing that
revelations in upon them.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:06.639
We witness Bev’s twisted view that God is
preparing his believers for the end of days

00:12:06.639 --> 00:12:09.769
and that the conversion will help them in
the perpetual night.

00:12:09.769 --> 00:12:15.160
Her truly awful nature is exposed as she turns
on Pruitt and won’t even feed on Hassan

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.309
believing his blood to be tainted.

00:12:17.309 --> 00:12:21.059
The converted have their hubris ruined it
for themselves by burning most of the places

00:12:21.059 --> 00:12:25.649
they could have hidden during the day and
we see Erin, Sarah and Hassan navigate to

00:12:25.649 --> 00:12:29.350
the only hiding spots left to bring them down
in a blaze of glory.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:34.889
It shows they are truly sinful and just like
Lucifer, their gift has been taken away damning

00:12:34.889 --> 00:12:37.050
them to burn alive come dawn.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:42.480
Pride and hubris is one of God's most hated
traits according to the Bible so he does truly

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.160
give and take away.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.239
In the end For all his sins, Pruitt saw the
error of his ways and finally spoke to his

00:12:49.239 --> 00:12:51.749
daughter without the burden of hiding the
truth.

00:12:51.749 --> 00:12:56.500
He realized that he had lost his way and just
before this, the fundamental difference between

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.619
Bev and Pruitt was exposed.

00:12:58.619 --> 00:13:02.259
She saw the church as being an ark and a base
to spread the conversion.

00:13:02.259 --> 00:13:06.399
He explains it was about God and he wanted
to do right by his community except Bev has

00:13:06.399 --> 00:13:11.010
taken it to the extreme and accuses him of
switching to ‘human things’ and not the

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.010
divine.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:17.230
In reality, the hole he felt in his life has
been filled as he can now acknowledge his

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.489
secret sin.

00:13:18.489 --> 00:13:22.330
He can finally leave the church, which he
wanted to all these years and end his life

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.910
on his terms with his family around him.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:28.369
Now one question you might have is did the
angel die?

00:13:28.369 --> 00:13:34.439
As Erin lays there dying she manages to cut
his wings as he feast on her neck.

00:13:34.439 --> 00:13:39.269
Warren explains that the angel would need
to fly around 30 miles to beat the sun which

00:13:39.269 --> 00:13:41.009
would be very difficult for it.

00:13:41.009 --> 00:13:46.209
He’s unsure if the angel can make it the
distance but in the end we just don’t know.

00:13:46.209 --> 00:13:50.199
This creature has of course survived for centuries
and I don’t think that you can count it

00:13:50.199 --> 00:13:51.369
out either way.

00:13:51.369 --> 00:13:55.739
It’s very much a schrodingers angel but
I do think that thematically we can say that

00:13:55.739 --> 00:13:59.749
it’s gone too as it’s life was tied pretty
closely to the lives of islanders in the show.

00:13:59.749 --> 00:14:10.759
However there’s always the possibility there
if Flannagan wants to do a sequel.

00:14:10.759 --> 00:14:16.669
Now in the end we do have two survivors in
Warren and Leeza.

00:14:16.669 --> 00:14:21.459
After gaining Chekovs sniper rifle they managed
to flee the island on a boat in order to wait

00:14:21.459 --> 00:14:22.619
it out until dawn.

00:14:22.619 --> 00:14:27.139
Both were virtuous with Warren abstaining
from drink and Leeza showing forgiveness to

00:14:27.139 --> 00:14:29.220
Joe leading them to survive.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.699
Leeza cannot walk or feel her legs which is
of course due to the angel blood running out

00:14:33.699 --> 00:14:34.699
in her system.

00:14:34.699 --> 00:14:40.221
Now Leeza may be back to square one but she
has rejected false prophets, something that

00:14:40.221 --> 00:14:42.020
the bible has countless verses on.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.020
In a twist of irony, Bev says similar verses
to Paul when he starts to doubt turning his

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:44.020
flock into vampires and over the suggestion
burning down the town is a bad idea.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.020
Bev quotes Matthew 23:9 “And do not call
anyone on earth ‘father,’ for you have

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.020
one Father, and he is in heaven.”

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.020
Leeza and Warren’s escape could be looked
at as the rapture, escaping the damned Crockett

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:51.449
Island much like Christian’s say how the
believers will be saved and the rest left

00:14:51.449 --> 00:14:52.449
to judgement.

00:14:52.449 --> 00:14:57.319
The others had twisted their religion to justify
awful things and twisting the gift they were

00:14:57.319 --> 00:15:00.910
given, showing that humans have not really
changed that much from the original sin.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:01.910
However Riley preferred to end his eternal
life on his terms and could not abide by what

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:02.910
he would need to do, and sought redemption
in ending or trying to end what was going

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:03.910
to happen.

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:05.790
The survivors of Crockett sought peace in
the sun rise and look to wash themselves away

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.819
in the divine light of god.

00:15:07.819 --> 00:15:12.439
The bible itself said in Luke 1:78-79: “Because
of the tender mercy of our God, whereby the

00:15:12.439 --> 00:15:16.489
sunrise shall visit us from on high to give
light to those who sit in darkness and in

00:15:16.489 --> 00:15:19.730
the shadow of death, to guide our feet into
the way of peace.”

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:24.189
The sunrise is a symbolic nature that it is
a new day and the sins of the past are washed

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:25.189
away.

00:15:25.189 --> 00:15:28.929
We also see the ash of their bodies blow over
the boat and this is very symbolic of the

00:15:28.929 --> 00:15:33.389
saying ‘ashes to ashes’ and ‘dust to
‘dust’ which of course pulls from the

00:15:33.389 --> 00:15:34.389
bible.

00:15:34.389 --> 00:15:38.679
As they die everyone on the island sings nearer
my god to thee and this has significance for

00:15:38.679 --> 00:15:39.999
a number of reasons.

00:15:39.999 --> 00:15:45.019
Firstly it contains lyrics about angels beckoning
those on Earth into Heaven and how they will

00:15:45.019 --> 00:15:46.359
finally meet God.

00:15:46.359 --> 00:15:51.180
However it was also the last song to be played
on the Titanic as it and it's passengers sunk

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.480
into the ocean to their deaths.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:56.480
Though it should be seen as a tragic ending
for Leeza she has very much avoided the easy

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:01.600
road and though she is back to being paralysed
she is still alive, unlike all the others

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.499
who gave into sin and the temptation of a
better life.

00:16:04.499 --> 00:16:08.110
Her defeating this tempation and breaking
away from the flock is what saves her life

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.670
in the end and it stands firm as a positive
message.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:15.610
The series shows us that the road to hell
is paved with good intentions and though she

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:20.009
could have given in at any point due to pressure
from her parents, an authority figure and

00:16:20.009 --> 00:16:23.050
her community, she didn’t and thus now gets
to live.

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:28.019
In the end it’s has a very powerful meaning
and overall the show was a stunning work of

00:16:28.019 --> 00:16:31.429
acting, writing and the portrayal of a wide
range of beliefs.

00:16:31.429 --> 00:16:36.249
This was merged into a layered and nuanced
view on the spectrum of belief and religion

00:16:36.249 --> 00:16:37.740
that is a real page turner.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:45.139
I know that phrasing doesn’t work here but
you know what I mean, it was an easy binge.

00:16:45.139 --> 00:16:51.169
It’s something each viewer will take their
own meaning from, just like the good book.

00:16:51.169 --> 00:16:56.019
While Midnight Mass is a wild departure from
The Haunting series and though some may take

00:16:56.019 --> 00:17:01.089
a time to adjust to it, it is an absolutely
outstanding series that I can’t praise high

00:17:01.089 --> 00:17:02.089
enough.

00:17:02.089 --> 00:17:05.120
It’s rare that we give shows or films a
10/10

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:09.819
Now obviously I’d love to hear your thoughts
on the show and what you took from it as I

00:17:09.819 --> 00:17:14.069
know a lot of people will have different views
on the series.

